From 649d9434977b52357f28fd69d99fef19477de9d2 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Hao Lin <hao.lin@samsung.com>
Date: Wed, 4 Nov 2026 22:05:40 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 7/9] compaction: send a textual sysctl trigger

Writing the binary representation of int 1 violates the sysctl integer
parser and can fail without triggering compaction. Send the one-byte
textual value and require that byte to be accepted. Keep n for the
existing zone loop; do not change compaction policy.

Based on analysis of He Fangyu's fix 16d6125d
---
 src/resource-optimizer/memory/compaction.c | 7 ++-----
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 5 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/resource-optimizer/memory/compaction.c b/src/resource-optimizer/memory/compaction.c
index 4b5fec3..d060cfc 100644
--- a/src/resource-optimizer/memory/compaction.c
+++ b/src/resource-optimizer/memory/compaction.c
@@ -218,11 +218,8 @@ static void compaction_start(struct compact_control *compact)
 		_E("Compaction: failed to open procfs entry [%d]\n", errno);
 		goto leave;
 	}
-	/*
-	 * It doesn't really matter what gets written,
-	 * as long as smth gets....
-	 */
-	if (write(fd, &n, sizeof(n)) <= 0)
+	/* compact_memory is a textual integer sysctl. */
+	if (write(fd, "1", 1) != 1)
 		current_status |= COMPACT_FAILURE;
 	/*
 	 * Reset the external fragmentation warnings.
